<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105803" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρωκ-τός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be gnawed</i> or <i>eaten raw; eatable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.92
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῆποι τ.</span>
			<i>kitchen</i> gardens, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				3.56
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. λάχανα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Artem.
					1.67
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρωκτά, τά,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρωγάλια</span>
			, <i>fruits eaten at dessert,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσα ἐστὶ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.3.12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρωκτὰ σησάμου τε καὶ μέλιτος</span>
			<i>sweatmeats</i> of sesame and honey, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.48
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
